WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.040 --> 00:00:04.820
How does a cancer arise?

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.250
When I started my research, no one could possibly tell you 

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.880
how that problem might be solved.

00:00:12.230 --> 00:00:12.750
And yet,

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.550
within a few years, it was solved,

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:19.790
beginning with something as humble as a chicken virus.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:24.670
We've come an extraordinary long way in our 

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:29.170
understanding of cancer in the span of my career,

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:31.050
which is 48 years or so,

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.600
but we've faced very daunting 

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:37.760
challenges.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.550
We are far from home free,

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:46.220
and it's going to take an unanticipated,

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.790
unpredictable breakthrough,

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:48.250
I think,

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:50.450
to get us home free.

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:51.660
In fact,

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:52.870
I'm a bit of a skeptic.

00:00:53.360 --> 00:00:57.580
I'm not sure we will ever cure metastatic cancer 

00:00:57.740 --> 00:00:58.550
uniformly.

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:04.150
I believe that the way we will ultimately manage cancer is by prevention.

00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:11.050
That's a lesson we learn from microbiology.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.150
Vaccines are better than antibiotics,

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:16.750
right?

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:21.740
You get resistance to antibiotics, that's become a major plague in 

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:23.350
humankind,

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.150
but vaccines prevent the infection to begin with.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:32.520
We know that we can prevent a lot of lung cancer by eliminating 

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:37.730
the use of tobacco. We know that we can prevent a 

00:01:37.730 --> 00:01:42.550
lot of skin cancer by limiting exposure to the ultraviolet light in sun.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:47.840
We know that we can prevent liver cancer by vaccinating against 

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.550
hepatitis viruses.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:53.710
We know that we can prevent cervical cancer by vaccinating against 

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:55.690
another virus.

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:57.250
Ultimately,

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:01.150
we could vanquish cancer by prevention.

00:02:02.295 --> 00:02:05.525
But we know so little about what causes cancer.

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.865
We do not know what causes breast cancer,

00:02:08.215 --> 00:02:09.085
colon cancer,

00:02:09.325 --> 00:02:10.395
pancreatic cancer,

00:02:10.405 --> 00:02:15.305
ovarian cancer, some of the major killers, we simply do not know what causes them.

00:02:15.695 --> 00:02:18.505
And it is a very difficult form of research.

00:02:19.735 --> 00:02:24.335
So I like to sound a cautionary note that we may 

00:02:24.335 --> 00:02:27.995
never conquer this disease completely with therapeutics.

00:02:27.995 --> 00:02:30.305
We will definitely improve how well we do,

00:02:30.315 --> 00:02:32.755
but we will not conquer the disease completely.

00:02:33.125 --> 00:02:36.225
We can conquer it ultimately through prevention.

